metric=p['metrics_by_profile']['F256'];ratioCH=by['CH','F256']['cycles']/by['CH','P0']['cycles'];lines=['# scalarProd-F256: closed four-source negative-CH response','', '**Fixed as-of:** source-qualified provider2026-11-04 10:16:09 Asia/Shanghai (02:16:09UTC), snapshot20261104T021610149488Z_429a0980. Only CH-P0/CH-F256/DH-P0/DH-F256 are analyzed. CH-F128 is AWAIT_ROOT_RESULT in this captured context; no six-cell or F128 performance is fabricated. The upstream context may show a legitimate old DH-F128 reference, but it is not consumed for this comparison.','', '**Finding:** CH regresses1,535cycles (+0.3651%) while DH improves1,828cycles (-0.4448%). Both designs have unchanged read request/miss/DRAM-read volume and lower L2 retry/admission events. Nevertheless, direct existing raw observations show higher FR-FCFS pending-queue occupancy and a heavier MRQ request-latency tail in both designs. This is a useful negative-CH case, not proof the tail caused its regression: DH becomes slightly faster despite the same tail direction.','', '## Exact identity, scale and kernel scope','', 'Frozen input `2b93f70cd0666c5112f5550aae7b3a8d0565de1de40604d494bdc36c503f6954`. Actual declared-body qualification and strict/raw/header evidence: one `_Z13scalarProdGPUPfS_S_ii` kernel, grid(128,1,1),block(256,1,1),128CTAs, shared4096bytes,23register header,730,610,912active-thread instructions, stream0. All four sources match this exact order/extent and build. Actual HtoD commands copy57,016,320bytes for each input array, total114,032,640bytes.','', 'Fixed Atlas47a097aad4406893a07f8d230e1e0a850609bf39 maps the candidate at app commitb059fdae25c2aabf737486aada743fca114469ce: scalarProd.cu parses13920as VECTOR_N and fixes ELEMENT_N1024; therefore candidate scale is13,920dot products of1024elements. This agrees with copy sizes and header but does not newly certify original numeric bytes/ELF.128CTAs must not be mistaken for128output vectors: the candidate CTA loops vec=blockIdx+128*r, handling108or109vectors.','', 'Candidate `kernel.cu:34-79` loads four accumulator positions per thread then performs a1024-element shared reduction for each vector; read/accumulate/reduction phases repeat across vectors/CTAs and overlap acrossCTAs. No separate reduction kernel exists. Existing perf CSV has exactly one terminal row in each run, with no intermediate source-phase timestamp. GPU sim_cycle+tot_cycle and sim_insn+tot_insn sums reconcile; the perf row precedes cumulative folding (tot fields0), so tot_cycle0is not zero execution. Consequently only the whole single kernel is measured; source-level read/reduction phases cannot be assigned separate measured cycles or queues.','', '## Cycles and relative-benefit interpretation','',tab(['Source','Kernel cycles = whole replay','Delta vs same-design P0'],[[c+'-'+pf,by[c,pf]['cycles'],by[c,pf]['cycles']-by[c,'P0']['cycles']]for c,pf in pairs]),'',tab(['Metric','Value'],[[k,metric[k]]for k in['S_CH','S_DH','R_P0','R','I']]),'',f"I factorization = {ratioCH:.9f} (CH cycle-regression factor) * {metric['S_DH']:.9f} (DH own speedup) = {metric['I']:.9f}. Relative improvement0.8134% includes both CH deterioration and DH small gain; it is not0.8134% DH self-speedup. Same-F CH/DH1.031358 favors DH in this one input/configuration, with architecture/cost differences preserved. No partial-suite GM or unified configuration choice is made.",'', '## Read/write traffic and L2/admission events','', 'L2 GLOBAL accepted/miss quantities are32-byte sectors; DRAM read/write quantities are issued32-byte atoms. DRAM n_req/MRQ histogram counts are request objects: a128-byte writeback may issue4atoms. Do not equate these populations.','',tab(['Counter','CH-P0','CH-F256','DH-P0','DH-F256'],[[label,*[by[k]['totals'].get(field)for k in pairs]]for field,label in[('L2_GLOBAL_read_accepted_sectors','GLOBAL accepted read sectors'),('L2_GLOBAL_read_miss_sectors','GLOBAL read misses'),('L2_total_cache_misses','All-L2 misses, incl writes'),('DRAM_read_atoms32B','DRAM read atoms32B'),('DRAM_write_atoms32B','DRAM write atoms32B'),('DRAM_controller_n_req','DRAM request objects'),('L2_total_cache_reservation_fails','L2 reservation retry events'),('gpu_stall_dramfull','ICNT-to-memory blocked admission events')]]),'', 'All GLOBAL accepted reads are misses in these observations, with3,563,520read sectors/DRAM read atoms =114,032,640bytes, equal to the two input-copy sizes. This is observed access behavior under the fixed replay, not a compulsory/capacity/conflict or cold-miss classification. The write miss count is1,740sectors for all four runs. CH adds4issued write atoms at F256; DH write count is unchanged. Issued writes are not proof of complete final dirty-cache drain.','',tab(['L2 GLOBAL-read retry reason','CH-P0','CH-F256','DH-P0','DH-F256'],[[reason,*[by[k]['kernels'][0]['positive_only_retry_reasons'].get('L2_cache_stats_fail_breakdown:GLOBAL_ACC_R:'+reason)for k in pairs]]for reason in['MISS_QUEUE_FULL','MSHR_ENRTY_FAIL','MSHR_MERGE_ENRTY_FAIL']]),'', 'Entry-capacity retries and miss-queue retries fall in both designs; unprinted merge-list reasons remain MISSING, not imputed0. Events do not measure stalled cycles, queue occupancy or critical-path time. The legacy gpu_stall_dramfull is ICNT admission, not isolated DRAM-queue wait. No time-average/peak L2 miss-queue occupancy is available in these logs; each of the40L2 miss-queue terminal dumps is explicitly empty, a terminal gauge only.','', '## Existing raw DRAM queue observations: occupancy, not latency','', 'Fixed Core dram.cc:323-346 samples FR-FCFS num_pending after scheduling once per dram_t::cycle; ave_mrqs/n_cmd is the cumulative per-controller pending-request mean over all DRAM ticks (including idle/launch ticks). The peak is sampled at that same after-scheduler point. It excludes active bank service and is not L2 MSHR occupancy or a request-duration mean. Raw queue_avg is printed with decimals; mrqq:max/avg is a second view. Both were parsed and crosschecked without modifying strict metrics/reader.','',tab(['Source','Mean pending / controller / DRAM tick','Controller mean range','Highest sampled peak over20controllers','DRAM ACT/PRE counts'],[[c+'-'+pf,qb[c,pf]['aggregate']['pooled_queue_pending_mean_per_controller_per_DRAM_tick_from_printed_floats'],str(qb[c,pf]['aggregate']['queue_mean_range_over_controllers']),qb[c,pf]['aggregate']['maximum_sampled_queue_peak_over_controllers'],str(qb[c,pf]['aggregate']['n_act_sum'])+'/'+str(qb[c,pf]['aggregate']['n_pre_sum'])]for c,pf in pairs]),'', 'The pooled mean weights each printed controller mean by its n_cmd; all20controllers share equal n_cmd within a run, so this also equals the simple controller mean up to printed precision. Occupancy rises from37.8535to41.2383inCH and39.6388to43.7268inDH. Peaks rise64to237/243. The accumulator\'s maximum-sample*n_cmd bound is below2^32for every controller here, so unsigned ave_mrqs overflow cannot explain these particular values. Larger occupancy does not establish a corresponding critical-load delay or explain the opposite total-cycle signs.','', 'Read atom totals are exactly balanced across20controllers (read-volume CV0). Each controller has4of16nonzero printed bank-read-command counters. The fixed source increments this field onRD only; it does not imply the other banks had no write activity, prove a bank bottleneck, or identify mapping as the cause. Dirty writeback/order, bank service and credit occupancy are not causally separated.','', '## Latency histogram and extrema, with exact units/windows','', 'All four strict mean latency dictionaries are{} and raw means are suppressed. Single-kernel cycles are below500,000; fixed print-before-stat-fold ordering can leave num_mfs0and suppress the mean block even though other counters are populated. Missing means remain MISSING, never0. Decimal queue_avg is an occupancy metric, not an unparsed average latency.','', 'Existing mrq_lat_table contains32explicit floor-log2 bins. Fixed dram_req_t timestamps request construction in global core cycles; dram_sched.cc records elapsed time when the request is assigned to a bank. Thus this spans staging/FR-FCFS scheduling to bank assignment, not complete L2-to-DRAM service or a known critical load. The histogram sums exactly to controller n_req in every run, about3.564millionrequest objects; all terminal DRAM latency queues are empty. It is independent of the num_mfs print gate.','',tab(['Source','MRQ request samples','Fraction>=512core cycles %','Fraction>=1024cycles %','Median bucket bounds','p99.9bucket bounds','Mean bounds only'],[[c+'-'+pf,qb[c,pf]['MRQ_latency_histogram']['n'],100*qb[c,pf]['MRQ_latency_histogram']['fraction_ge_512_core_cycles'],100*qb[c,pf]['MRQ_latency_histogram']['fraction_ge_1024_core_cycles'],str(qb[c,pf]['MRQ_latency_histogram']['median_bounds']['core_cycle_bounds']),str(qb[c,pf]['MRQ_latency_histogram']['p999_bounds']['core_cycle_bounds']),str(qb[c,pf]['MRQ_latency_histogram']['derived_mean_core_cycle_bounds'])]for c,pf in pairs]),'', 'P99.9 moves from the256-511bucket to512-1023in both designs. The>=512cycle share grows CH0.0603%to0.6142% andDH0.0449%to0.6235%. These are request-tail facts, not a claim the median doubled or the tail lies on the critical path. P0/F256 derived mean intervals overlap; the bins do not yield an exact mean or prove its increase. No midpoint is substituted for an observed average.','',tab(['Source','maxMRQ','maxMF','maxICNT-to-memory','maxICNT-to-shader'],[[c+'-'+pf,*[qb[c,pf]['reported_max_core_cycle_diagnostics'].get(k)for k in['maxmrqlatency','maxmflatency','max_icnt2mem_latency','max_icnt2sh_latency']]]for c,pf in pairs]),'', 'MRQ/MF extrema rise while max ICNT-to-memory falls. These are different event populations/segments; they must not be subtracted into DRAM service time or treated as average delay. Longer request tails are consistent with the larger window/credit behavior, but DH\'s slight speedup despite that direction prevents a simple tail-to-total-cycle causal story.','', '## Typed frontend/finite service and source limits','', 'CH PAPER_BASE uses common PIB256; DH PAPER_OO uses its active PIB128, while generic PIB8 is inactive for OO admission. CH common Tag-conflict attempts remain2,672,640, PIB-full events0and per-SM PIB peak32; ordinary L1 entry/merge-full events are0. They are not OO measurements. DH OO PIB-full/Tag-conflict event counters remain unprinted/null.','', 'DH has890,880new read-line misses/lower128B creations and0valid/0pending line hits in both profiles; accepted L2 read sectors equal4*890,880. Hence no measured OO read-line reuse or request-count reduction explains the small DH gain here. The candidate has no inter-vector input overlap, but static source addresses are not substituted for runtime classifications.','',tab(['DH profile','Mean PIB entries, all64SM samples','Mean physical lines','Ready-to-retire cycles / retired entry','Writeback wait sum'],[[x['profile'],x['DH_finite_service']['mean_PIB_entries_all64SM_samples'],x['DH_finite_service']['mean_physical_lines_all64SM_samples'],x['DH_finite_service']['fully_ready_to_complete_cycles_per_retired_read_entry'],x['DH_finite_service']['cumulative']['DTC_SERVICE_V1_wb_wait']]for x in service if x['cell']=='DH']),'', 'Ready-to-complete and writeback sums slightly rise even as DH cycles fall; these all-entry/sample sums and means are not critical-path timing or per-SM peaks. Low mean PIB usage does not exclude bursts or dependency pressure. Cross-design L1/Tag/physical pool/queue/timing/area remain unequal.','', 'Within each design only FR-FCFS64to256changes, and the fixed Core couples shared-credit255to447with it (return queue192,two subpartitions). DRAM850MHz, Core/ICNT/L2 clocks,10MiB L2/mapping and frontend mechanism remain fixed. This is queue-window plus credit expansion, not an isolated queue-capacity intervention or equal-area claim.','', '## Facts, association and unconfirmed cause','', '- Fact: one measured kernel; CH negative/DH small positive; fixed read volume, fewer retries/ICNT admission events, higher FR pending occupancy and heavier MRQ tail. No F128 result is fabricated.','- Source deduction: repeated per-vector global reads plus shared reduction/barriers; fixed active window/credit and sampling/print semantics. Original capture ELF/numeric linkage remains unconfirmed.','- Association: the larger coupled window changes queue occupancy and request tails while total cycles move differently across designs.','- Unconfirmed: critical-request identity, bank/credit/return-path occupancy histories, and whether memory-stage versus shared-reduction/issue/finite-service timing determines the1535/-1828cycle changes. Existing one-terminal-row perf data cannot split those phases. No new instrumentation, rerun, additional model or configuration is launched.','', '## Evidence','', 'SOURCE_SNAPSHOT_RECEIPT.json and CAPTURED_SOURCE_QUALIFIED_PROVIDER.json pin the actual qualified snapshot7bd245cec0b447aa73461676078c08afb4fd633e3db3c0e681f9f03b5fbb695a/providerb2ccd243963c7a355b11f93cdcaef6e0b9028ca9e89fe01edbb2247661007626. Old source roles and actual profiles are retained. V1_PARSER_CONSUMPTION.json proves all28V1members unchanged and records the exact reused parser SHA; current child adapts only scalarProd/P0/F256 filtering. FORWARD_EVIDENCE_BOUNDARIES.md preserves reviewer terminology: read-active, no unproved cold/miss class or request-origin attribution.','', 'CLOSED_SOURCE_KERNEL_COUNTERS.json.gz contains four RESULT/raw/exit/input SHA and whole-kernel explicit endpoints; RAW_QUEUE_AND_LATENCY_HISTOGRAM.json contains all20controller values/bins/derived bounds/quantiles; QUEUE_LATENCY_FIXED_SOURCE_SEMANTICS.json pins Core9eed paths/SHA/line excerpts. ACTUAL_INPUT_CONTRACT.json and EXISTING_WITHIN_KERNEL_OBSERVABILITY.json retain actual geometry/body count and each closed terminal CSV SHA. FIXED_ATLAS_SCALARPROD.md is exact Atlas47a source candidate documentation.16parser/identity checks plus352queue/hist checks pass (368counted checks); additional typed/header/perf assertions are recorded by their evidence. No live raw, reader/native/owner/registry/Git/paper change.','',tab(['Source','Role','RESULT path','RESULT SHA256','Raw gzip SHA256'],[[c+'-'+pf,by[c,pf]['source_role'],by[c,pf]['RESULT_path'],by[c,pf]['RESULT_sha256'],by[c,pf]['raw_gzip_sha256']]for c,pf in pairs]),'']
